ion, while executable changes retain their required suite and checks. Preserve actual source/check/review evidence.\n\n### Handoff\n\nUse the [shared worker handoff](README.md#worker-handoff). Verify and record this ticket's completion without treating it as milestone acceptance. Select further work only through the [published milestone plan](milestones.md); do not start the next ticket automatically.\n\n### Comments\n\n#### QA realignment\n\nReconciled with approved slice R17; the [previous definition](archive/issues-before-milestone-qa/14-verify-role-write-boundaries.md) is retained for history. This revision supersedes the old product-first execution order without reopening completed tickets 01\u201309.\n\n<!-- Proposed publication: issues/30-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md -->\n\n<a id=\"r18-run-a-generated-approved-plan-through-the-runtime\"></a>\n\n## 30: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime\n\n**What to build:** Complete the remaining integration portion of pre-QA ticket 15. Produce a small plan through the unified skill, validate it against the now-implemented milestone/skill contracts, and execute it through the scripted public seam. Demonstrate project-default guidance and a role-specific ticket addition, preserving required contracts.\n\n**Blocked by:** [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md); [21: Execute approved QA corrections](issues/21-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md); [25: Capture and deliver selected local skills](issues/25-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md).\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n**Plan version:** [oop-v1](spec.md).\n\n**Milestone:** M4. Follow [milestone eligibility](milestones.md) before selecting work.\n\n**Plan slice:** [R18](ticket-proposal.md#r18-run-a-generated-approved-plan-through-the-runtime).\n\n**Agent context limit:** 250,000 tokens of active context. Use the [agent context policy](README.md#agent-context-policy).\n\n**Worker reasoning:** Medium by default; an explicit ticket override applies to implementation and repair. Spec and Standards review default to High with independent role configuration.\n\n**Role guidance:** Inherit the development role defaults in [Role Configuration](spec.md#role-configuration); no ticket-specific additions. Preserve this ticket's existing runtime role/skill requirements.\n\n**Context:** [planning and milestone contract](spec.md#planning-and-milestone-contract); [skill selection and delivery](spec.md#skill-selection-and-delivery).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Generate a small human-approved spec/ticket/milestone bundle through the unified planning skill and validate it against the implemented canonical contracts.\n- [ ] Demonstrate explicit project defaults and an applicable role-specific ticket addition, plus a ticket requiring no additions, preserving mandatory role guidance.\n- [ ] Run the approved example through intentional scripted CLI execution, reaching planned QA and exact local promotion with captured/delivered instruction identities.\n- [ ] Keep publishing distinct from execution and QA planning distinct from acceptance; preserve original inputs and evidence.\n- [ ] Include interfaces, invariants, testing seams, Pythonic shared design, and appropriate test strategy without replaying all selection validation already covered by ticket 25.\n\n### Verification\n\nA generated example reaches QA and promotion with recorded selection/content identities. Planning publication does not itself launch execution; the example uses an explicit run.\n\nFollow the repository's testing policy; document-only skill changes use skill/link/workflow validation, while executable changes retain their required suite and checks. Preserve actual source/check/review evidence.\n\n### Handoff\n\nUse the [shared worker handoff](README.md#worker-handoff). Verify and record this ticket's completion without treating it as milestone acceptance. Select further work only through the [published milestone plan](milestones.md); do not start the next ticket automatically.\n\n<!-- Proposed publication: issues/31-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md -->\n\n<a id=\"r19-demonstrate-the-revised-first-usable-release\"></a>\n\n## 31: Demonstrate the revised first usable release\n\n**What to build:** Expand pre-QA ticket 16's clean-checkout acceptance to planning, background operation, two QA milestones, corrections, safe checkpoint continuation, exact local promotions, blocked/waiting work, optional findings, selected guidance, and actual Codex/access evidence. Clearly document deferred concurrency, arbitrary crash recovery, hosted PRs/GitHub checks, and email.\n\n**Blocked by:** [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md); [22: Operate the orchestrator in the background](issues/22-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md); [23: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](issues/23-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md); [29: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](issues/29-verify-role-write-boundaries.md); [30: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](issues/30-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md); [07: Report optional review suggestions without rework](issues/07-report-optional-suggestions-without-repair.md).\n\n**Status:** ready-for-agent\n\n**Plan version:** [oop-v1](spec.md).\n\n**Milestone:** M4. Follow [milestone eligibility](milestones.md) before selecting work.\n\n**Plan slice:** [R19](ticket-proposal.md#r19-demonstrate-the-revised-first-usable-release).\n\n**Agent context limit:** 250,000 tokens of active context. Use the [agent context policy](README.md#agent-context-policy).\n\n**Worker reasoning:** Medium by default; an explicit ticket override applies to implementation and repair. Spec and Standards review default to High with independent role configuration.\n\n**Role guidance:** Inherit the development role defaults in [Role Configuration](spec.md#role-configuration); no ticket-specific additions. Preserve this ticket's existing runtime role/skill requirements.\n\n**Context:** [testing decisions](spec.md#testing-decisions); [out of scope](spec.md#out-of-scope).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Document installation, actual CLI/background/foreground/status/log/stop/continue interfaces, role settings, limits, requirements, skill selections and artifact/decision inspection.\n- [ ] Provide a clean-checkout disposable example covering two milestones, planned QA waits, explicit approval, correction-plan amendment, safe continuation and exact feature-to-dev promotion.\n- [ ] Retain repaired/blocked/dependent/unrelated/optional-finding examples and final feature acceptance without bypassing any QA boundary.\n- [ ] Run the complete deterministic suite and required static/packaging/installed CLI checks without routine model credentials or network access.\n- [ ] Retain actual small Codex/skill/access evidence or report its blocker; show immutable approved inputs and exact candidate-bound branch advancement.\n- [ ] Clearly separate sequential operation and planned-QA continuation from deferred concurrency, arbitrary crash recovery, hosted PR/GitHub checks, and email. Context experiment 28 is prioritized separately, not a release gate.\n\n### Verification\n\nRun the existing required complete suite and packaging/installed CLI checks, follow the documented disposable-repository walkthrough, and retain actual live evidence or its explicit blocker. Ticket 28 is scheduled early but is not a prerequisite for release acceptance.\n\nFollow the repository's testing policy; document-only skill changes use skill/link/workflow validation, while executable changes retain their required suite and checks. Preserve actual source/check/review evidence.\n\n### Handoff\n\nUse the [shared worker handoff](README.md#worker-handoff). Verify and record this ticket's completion without treating it as milestone acceptance. Select further work only through the [published milestone plan](milestones.md); do not start the next ticket automatically.\n\n### Comments\n\n#### QA realignment\n\nReconciled with approved slice R19; the [previous definition](archive/issues-before-milestone-qa/16-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) is retained for history. This revision supersedes the old product-first execution order without reopening completed tickets 01\u201309.\n\n## Prior decomposition and history\n\nExisting R01\u2013R19 retain the responsibilities and historical lineage in the [prior proposal](archive/before-oop-v1/ticket-proposal.md). New O01\u2013O03 add internal ownership work, without taking scope from later slices or reopening completed work. The [numbering map](archive/oop-numbering-history.md) governs current owner lookup; historical issue numbers in completion evidence remain historical.\n\n### Completed stable slices\n\nCompleted issue bodies keep their existing proposal anchors. Their work and evidence are unchanged:\n\n<a id=\"r01-turn-one-grilling-session-into-an-approved-plan\"></a>\n\n- R01: [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md) \u2014 completed; retain its original acceptance evidence.\n\n<a id=\"r02-stop-development-handoffs-at-human-checkpoints\"></a>\n\n- R02: [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md) \u2014 completed; retain its original acceptance evidence.\n\n<a id=\"r03-execute-only-the-first-eligible-milestone\"></a>\n\n- R03: [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md) \u2014 completed; retain its original acceptance evidence.\n\n<a id=\"r04-present-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate\"></a>\n\n- R04: [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md) \u2014 completed; retain its original acceptance evidence.\n\n<a id=\"r05-consume-approval-promote-and-continue\"></a>\n\n- R05: [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md) \u2014 completed; retain its original acceptance evidence.\n\n<a id=\"r06-continue-after-a-deliberate-qa-stop\"></a>\n\n- R06: [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md) \u2014 completed; retain its original acceptance evidence.\n\n<a id=\"comparison-with-the-pre-qa-open-tickets\"></a>\n\nThe [prior proposal](archive/before-oop-v1/ticket-proposal.md#comparison-with-the-pre-qa-open-tickets) retains the pre-QA decomposition comparison. Look up its current owners through this version's [numbering map](archive/oop-numbering-history.md).\n",
-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/milestones.md": "# Development milestones \u2014 OOP amendment\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v1. [Scope and change summary](ticket-proposal.md#change-summary). No milestone is accepted by this draft.\n\n## Eligibility and decisions\n\n- Completed 01\u201315 retain their identities and evidence. M1 is extended before its still-pending human QA; new M1 work is 16\u201318 in preferred order. Ticket 16 is the first proposed implementation after amendment publication, but planning does not start it.\n- Follow genuine dependencies inside the current milestone. Later release milestones wait for verified completion and explicit human acceptance of the preceding milestone. Stable milestone IDs M1\u2013M4 remain unchanged.\n- Development milestones govern this repository's work and are distinct from target-repository milestones exercised by fixtures. An approved plan, a passing test, a completed ticket or a scripted fixture decision never accepts a development candidate.\n- Actual QA uses request-specific evidence and a separate explicit human decision with the implemented candidate/input identities. No existing active run's approved inputs may be edited by publication; historical evidence and captures keep their original IDs.\n- E1 is independent; prioritize 28 immediately after verified 27, with its own final acceptance. It does not gate M3, M4 or release.\n\n## Required release membership\n\n| Milestone | Required tickets in preferred order | Entry gate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| M1: A complete QA-controlled Git cycle | [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md), [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md), [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md), [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md), [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md), [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md), [16: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues/16-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md), [17: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](issues/17-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md), [18: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](issues/18-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md) | First eligible milestone after amendment approval |\n| M2: An unattended operator workflow | [19: Guide a human through milestone QA](issues/19-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md), [20: Propose a versioned correction plan](issues/20-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md), [21: Execute approved QA corrections](issues/21-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md), [22: Operate the orchestrator in the background](issues/22-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md), [23: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](issues/23-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md) | Explicit human acceptance of M1 |\n| M3: Real agents with explicit guidance | [24: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](issues/24-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md), [25: Capture and deliver selected local skills](issues/25-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md), [26: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](issues/26-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md), [27: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](issues/27-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md) | Explicit human acceptance of M2 |\n| M4: First usable release and final acceptance | [29: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](issues/29-verify-role-write-boundaries.md), [30: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](issues/30-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md), [31: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](issues/31-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) | Explicit human acceptance of M3 |\n\nEvery required ticket 10\u201327 and 29\u201331 has exactly one required membership (21 tickets, including completed 10\u201315). Completed baseline 01\u201309 is preserved. Ticket 28 belongs only to E1. M4 is the final checkpoint with cumulative acceptance of all required work.\n\n## M1: A complete QA-controlled Git cycle\n\n**Required tickets:** [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md), [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md), [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md), [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md), [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md), [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md), [16: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues/16-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md), [17: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](issues/17-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md), [18: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](issues/18-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** Use a disposable repository with the existing foreground scripted two-milestone setup and the final refactored source. Inspect the approved planning output and development handoff, retained attempt/gate history from a repair or decision case, and a deliberate checkpoint produced by pre-refactor code.\n\n**Human actions:** Observe first-group integration into the feature branch, a regression-tested feature-to-dev candidate and a QA wait. Submit a stale approval and confirm dev/later-group work stay unchanged. Stop and continue in a new process; confirm completed assignments/baseline are not replayed and history persists. Approve the exact current request, confirm both refs advance only to its candidate, and observe later-group work start only then. Complete the final fixture QA; inspect correct attempt/ticket states and final-only feature completion. Assess the prior-code checkpoint continuation evidence and post-restore canonical-gate invalidation evidence.\n\n**Pass conditions:** All new refactor tickets are verified, the current source preserves the public CLI/record/checkpoint behavior, and observed identities agree with exact tested/accepted candidates. Refactor completion and scripted approvals alone do not accept the development milestone.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed harness/source/feature/development/candidate revisions, approved plan version and request identity, actual gate results and preserved artifacts, observed human checks, findings, and the explicit request-specific decision. Corrections require an approved amendment and renewed candidate acceptance; unchanged historical acceptance evidence retains its original scope.\n\n## M2: An unattended operator workflow\n\n**Required tickets:** [19: Guide a human through milestone QA](issues/19-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md), [20: Propose a versioned correction plan](issues/20-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md), [21: Execute approved QA corrections](issues/21-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md), [22: Operate the orchestrator in the background](issues/22-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md), [23: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](issues/23-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** After explicit M1 acceptance, use the QA-session guidance and a disposable plan with a correction and independent/dependent tickets; use separate operator sessions.\n\n**Human actions:** Request a correction, approve only its versioned amendment, inspect renewed QA, launch in the background, close the launching terminal, inspect status/logs and write the exact decision artifact separately. Observe blocked work alongside unrelated success while dependents and later milestones remain gated.\n\n**Pass conditions:** Correction approval is distinct from candidate acceptance; background operation remains inspectable; blocked roots do not block unrelated eligible work or unlock dependents/later milestones.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed harness/source/feature/development/candidate revisions, approved plan version and request identity, actual gate results and preserved artifacts, observed human checks, findings, and the explicit request-specific decision. Corrections require an approved amendment and renewed candidate acceptance; unchanged historical acceptance evidence retains its original scope.\n\n## M3: Real agents with explicit guidance\n\n**Required tickets:** [24: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](issues/24-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md), [25: Capture and deliver selected local skills](issues/25-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md), [26: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](issues/26-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md), [27: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](issues/27-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** After explicit M2 acceptance, prepare a tiny real-Codex case with project defaults, one applicable ticket addition and a worker override, preserving separate reviewer profiles.\n\n**Human actions:** Inspect combined design guidance, captured/delivered instruction identities, focused implementation/repair/Spec contexts and actual role settings/reports. Observe the real cycle and exact QA-controlled promotion. Schedule E1 immediately after verified 27 when its prerequisites are met.\n\n**Pass conditions:** Real process invocation and delivered instructions are evidenced; worker/repair use their agreed setting independently of High reviewers. Human approval stays separate from model output. E1 completion is not a condition of this milestone or release.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed harness/source/feature/development/candidate revisions, approved plan version and request identity, actual gate results and preserved artifacts, observed human checks, findings, and the explicit request-specific decision. Corrections require an approved amendment and renewed candidate acceptance; unchanged historical acceptance evidence retains its original scope.\n\n## M4: First usable release and final acceptance\n\n**Required tickets:** [29: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](issues/29-verify-role-write-boundaries.md), [30: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](issues/30-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md), [31: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](issues/31-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** After explicit M3 acceptance, start from a clean checkout and disposable target repository with the documented installed interfaces and retained access/real-agent evidence.\n\n**Human actions:** Inspect live role/file/ref/QA-authority probes and generated-plan execution. Operate planning, foreground/background launch, correction, status/logs, planned stop/continue, blocked/dependent/unrelated work, optional findings and two QA milestones. Inspect final exact development promotion and the documented deferred capabilities.\n\n**Pass conditions:** All required work from M1\u2013M4 is verified and its prior milestone acceptances are recorded; the current release passes the complete walkthrough and explicit final human acceptance. Ticket Done and all automated gates alone are insufficient. Coverage is cumulative across every required ticket 10\u201327 and 29\u201331, with completed baseline 01\u201309 preserved.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed harness/source/feature/development/candidate revisions, approved plan version and request identity, actual gate results and preserved artifacts, observed human checks, findings, and the explicit request-specific decision. Corrections require an approved amendment and renewed candidate acceptance; unchanged historical acceptance evidence retains its original scope.\n\n## E1: Independent early context experiment\n\n**Required tickets:** [28: Run the early context-budget comparison](issues/28-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** Immediately after verified 27 supplies the actual backend, configured role settings and usage artifacts, select experiment 28 independently of release milestones.\n\n**Human actions:** Review the controlled 100K, 150K, 200K and 250K runs, task-relevant pressure case, cumulative/cached usage versus active occupancy, compaction behavior, result quality and measured limitations.\n\n**Pass conditions:** Evidence distinguishes hard enforcement, compaction thresholds and advisory limits without inferring unsupported claims. This experiment has its own final acceptance and never becomes a release prerequisite.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed harness/source/feature/development/candidate revisions, approved plan version and request identity, actual gate results and preserved artifacts, observed human checks, findings, and the explicit request-specific decision. Corrections require an approved amendment and renewed candidate acceptance; unchanged historical acceptance evidence retains its original scope.\n",
-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/README.md": "# Ticket harness \u2014 proposed OOP amendment\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v1. [Complete proposal and change summary](ticket-proposal.md#change-summary). Publication approval is pending; this draft does not replace the current approved authoring files.\n\n| Document | Review purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| [spec.md](spec.md) | Complete requirements carried forward with ownership, compatibility and verification contracts. |\n| [ticket-proposal.md](ticket-proposal.md) | Complete bodies for every proposed open ticket 16\u201331, dependencies and defaults. |\n| [milestones.md](milestones.md) | Fixed membership, actionable QA and final cumulative acceptance. |\n| [numbering map](archive/oop-numbering-history.md) | Requested sequential renumbering and history/publication scope. |\n\n## Implementation status\n\nTickets 01\u201315 remain complete with their original identities and evidence. This draft adds three unimplemented tickets, 16\u201318, and shifts the 13 existing open tickets to 19\u201331: 16 open tickets total. M1 has six completed tickets (10\u201315) and three proposed open tickets (16\u201318). M1 human QA has not been requested or accepted. No M2 ticket is eligible before M1 acceptance.\n\nAfter approval/publication, the next proposed implementation is 16; 17 follows its verified attempt-lifecycle prerequisite, while 18 follows completed 15 and is third in preferred order. Planning approval does not start any implementation or harness run.\n\n## Complete ticket index\n\n| ID and title | Prerequisites | Readiness/completion | Milestone |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [01: Complete one scripted ticket through every gate](issues/01-complete-one-scripted-ticket-cycle.md) | None | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [02: Reject invalid requirements before starting work](issues/02-reject-invalid-inputs-before-execution.md) | 01 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [03: Reject invalid agent reports and review evidence](issues/03-validate-agent-reports-and-review-evidence.md) | 01 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [04: Promote only the exact verified candidate](issues/04-promote-only-the-verified-candidate.md) | 01 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [05: Repair rejected submissions within a bounded allowance](issues/05-repair-rejected-submissions-within-budget.md) | 03, 04 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [06: Stop for decisions outside approved contracts](issues/06-surface-human-decisions-without-retrying.md) | 05 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [07: Report optional review suggestions without rework](issues/07-report-optional-suggestions-without-repair.md) | 05 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [08: Stop stalled assignments and check processes](issues/08-stop-timed-out-process-trees.md) | 05 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [09: Execute verified dependencies in a stable order](issues/09-execute-dependencies-sequentially.md) | 02 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md) | 09 | completed | M1 |\n| [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md) | 10 | completed | M1 |\n| [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md) | 10 | completed | M1 |\n| [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md) | 12 | completed | M1 |\n| [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md) | 13 | completed | M1 |\n| [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md) | 14 | completed | M1 |\n| [16: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues/16-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md) | 05, 06 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [17: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](issues/17-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md) | 16 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [18: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](issues/18-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md) | 15 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [19: Guide a human through milestone QA](issues/19-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md) | 10, 14 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [20: Propose a versioned correction plan](issues/20-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md) | 10, 19 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [21: Execute approved QA corrections](issues/21-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md) | 15, 20 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [22: Operate the orchestrator in the background](issues/22-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md) | 15 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [23: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](issues/23-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md) | 12, 06 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [24: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](issues/24-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md) | 03 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [25: Capture and deliver selected local skills](issues/25-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md) | 10, 24 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [26: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](issues/26-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md) | 25 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [27: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](issues/27-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md) | 15, 26, 08 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [28: Run the early context-budget comparison](issues/28-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md) | 27 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | E1 |\n| [29: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](issues/29-verify-role-write-boundaries.md) | 19, 27 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M4 |\n| [30: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](issues/30-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md) | 10, 21, 25 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M4 |\n| [31: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](issues/31-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) | 11, 22, 23, 29, 30, 07 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M4 |\n\nReadiness is separate from dependency satisfaction and milestone eligibility. [Milestones](milestones.md) give preferred order: M1 10\u201318, M2 19\u201323, M3 24\u201327, independent E1 28 immediately after verified 27, then M4 29\u201331 subject to M3 acceptance. M4 requires final cumulative human acceptance of all required release work. E1 never gates release.\n\n## History\n\nThe [prior authoring bundle](archive/before-oop-v1/README.md) and [numbering map](archive/oop-numbering-history.md) preserve predecessor identities and approval scope. At publication archive the prior canonical documents and 13 open issue bodies before replacing their live authoring locations. Keep completed issue bodies, captured inputs, evidence and historical decision text unchanged. Current owner links may be updated without rewriting historical identities.\n\nThe completion evidence below is carried forward verbatim. Its next-ticket and milestone-state statements describe the time of that completion; this index's current Implementation status and versioned milestones govern new work.\n\n## Agent context policy\n\n- Use GPT-6.1 Sol as requested, with one fresh context for each implementation, review, or repair assignment.\n- Target at most **250,000 tokens of active context per agent**, including instructions, relevant source, tool results, reasoning/output retained in context, and room to finish verification and the handoff.\n- This is a per-agent context constraint, not a cumulative per-ticket usage budget. Reprocessing cached input across requests can make cumulative usage much larger than the currently occupied context.\n- Read the assigned issue and its scoped spec references first. Follow the repository's glossary/ADR instructions, discover the affected source, and pull extra references when necessary. Sibling transcripts and entire upstream skill libraries are not default inputs.\n- Keep headroom for debugging and final checks. If the bounded outcome will not fit, preserve useful work and report the evidence and proposed split before expanding the assignment.\n- No numerical implementation-usage estimate is claimed before measurements exist. These slices are scoped by observable outcomes and the context required to understand them.\n- The current local Codex catalog reports 500,000 nominal tokens and a 95% effective-window setting for gpt-6.1-sol; the inspected session reports a 475,000 effective window. The requested 8M figure was clarified to a 250K agent target after distinguishing cumulative usage from active context.\n- The 250K target guides the agents implementing these issues. Configurable runtime context controls and empirical comparison belong to the early live-backend experiment below; this document does not claim that a new hard runtime cap has already been implemented.\n\n## Worker handoff\n\nStart from the latest integrated prerequisite work. Read the current interface and evidence needed for this issue rather than replaying prior development conversations. Work on this issue's acceptance behavior and test at the public CLI/Git/report seam described by the spec.\n\nReturn a compact report with the outcome, commit references/changed files, actual check commands and exit results, and remaining decisions or risks. Preserve verbose logs as artifacts and link to them when needed.\n\nDuring approved harness execution, source specs and tickets remain unchanged and the harness owns execution records. A ready-for-agent label or published ticket alone does not start a run. Concurrency, arbitrary interruption/crash recovery, hosted PRs, and email remain deferred. Planned-QA checkpoint stop/continuation is implemented by ticket 15; development M1 and final feature human acceptance remain pending.\n\n## Early context-budget experiment\n\n[28: Compare configurable 100K\u2013250K agent context limits](issues/28-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md) is ready for execution immediately after issue 27 supplies the verified real Codex cycle, configured roles, and usage artifacts. Prioritize it then; it does not require the final release demonstration, multi-ticket scheduling, the planning skill, or the later access-boundary probes. It is a separate early experiment, not an additional first-release completion gate.\n\nThe user requested configurable per-agent limits of **100K, 150K, 200K, and 250K**. Compare the same workload, model, role reasoning settings, and acceptance checks at each setting. Record verified results, repair behavior, observed active context, compaction/handoff behavior, elapsed time, and cumulative/cached usage separately.\n\nUse a short control to verify configuration and reporting, plus a task-relevant case that can approach the configured context thresholds. If all runs remain below 100K, they cannot establish the comparative effects of the larger budgets.\n\nVerify whether the installed backend enforces a hard limit, applies a compaction threshold, or only supports advisory guidance. Report that distinction explicitly rather than interpreting cumulative input totals as window occupancy or claiming unsupported enforcement.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\n- [01: Complete one scripted ticket through every gate \u2014 completed](evidence/01-completion.md): implementation `b09e324`, final implementation `1666920`; 8 passing tests and passing checks; separate independent Spec and Standards reviews completed. [Actual fixture observations](evidence/01-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/01-complete-one-scripted-ticket-cycle.md#comments) record the passing and rejected runs. Later tickets and first-release completion remain outstanding.\n\n- [02: Reject invalid requirements before starting work \u2014 completed](evidence/02-completion.md): checkpoint `855a4c8`, review fixes `dfdb1a6` and final implementation `b11fd20`; 73 passing tests and passing checks; separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews passed. [Actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/02-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/02-reject-invalid-inputs-before-execution.md#comments) provide criterion-specific evidence. Eligibility validation is complete; dependency scheduling and later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [03: Reject invalid agent reports and review evidence \u2014 completed](evidence/03-completion.md): checkpoint `5b04187`, review fixes `2a27565` and final implementation `07094fa`; 256 passing tests and passing documented checks; independent Spec and Standards reviews passed with no remaining findings. [Actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/03-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/03-validate-agent-reports-and-review-evidence.md#comments) verify all six criteria. Report validation is complete; the subsequent transaction slice is recorded below. Repairs, broader human-decision handling, and later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [04: Promote only the exact verified candidate \u2014 completed](evidence/04-completion.md): checkpoint `dc27eb2`, final implementation/review fixes `8d345bd`; **304 passing tests** and passing documented checks; separate independent Spec and Standards re-reviews passed with no outstanding findings. [16 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/04-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/04-promote-only-the-verified-candidate.md#comments) verify all six criteria. Approved-input/state integrity, source approval invalidation, and exact candidate promotion are complete within the documented process-boundary limits. Automatic repairs and later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [05: Repair rejected submissions within a bounded allowance \u2014 completed](evidence/05-completion.md): implementation `34a49b7`; **362 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, packaging/installed CLI, and [20 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/05-fixture-observations.json) passed. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no issues. All six criteria verify configurable bounded repairs, fresh assignments with preserved rejection evidence, renewed exact-revision gates, and preserved Blocked/incomplete exhaustion. No unchecked criteria or unresolved ticket-05 items remain. Human-decision handling and neighboring later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [06: Stop for decisions outside approved contracts \u2014 completed](evidence/06-completion.md): implementation `dc1018e`; **399 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, packaging/installed CLI run/status, and [19 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/06-fixture-observations.json) passed. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no issues; Spec independently passed all 37 decision tests. All five criteria verify validated implementation/either-axis decisions, precise preserved contract/evidence/work handoffs, immediate stopping with repair allowance available, unchanged approved inputs/integration, and matching status/final output with accurate initial/later-repair history. No unchecked criteria or unresolved ticket-06 items remain. Optional-suggestion reporting and other later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [07: Report optional review suggestions without rework \u2014 completed](evidence/07-completion.md): checkpoint `83d361d`; **421 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, packaging/installed CLI and [23 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/07-fixture-observations.json) passed. Existing runtime behavior satisfied the ticket; 22 new cases and public contracts verify optional-only integration without consuming available repairs, full evidence/revision retention, mixed-finding repairs/exhaustion, changing suggestions across revisions, validation and human-decision compatibility. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no blockers; Spec independently passed 12 cases. Standards recorded one optional test-fixture consolidation suggestion. All five criteria are verified; no unchecked criteria or required unresolved items remain. Timeouts and neighboring later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [08: Stop stalled assignments and check processes \u2014 completed](evidence/08-completion.md): implementation `fbfc088`; **448 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, wheel/install and installed CLI passed. [27 actual timeout-test observations plus installed CLI smoke](evidence/08-fixture-observations.json) verify positive stage allowances, inherited process-group/child cleanup, partial output, timeout precedence over report claims/zero leader exits, fresh bounded repairs and exact integration, exhaustion, baseline/environment stopping and durable status evidence. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no blockers; Spec independently verified background-child cleanup after normal completion. Standards recorded optional S1 about streaming output to reduce memory use. All six criteria are verified; no unchecked criteria or required unresolved items remain. Scheduling/continuation, live Codex/role guidance, OS role enforcement and recovery remain later tickets.\n\n- [09: Execute verified dependencies in a stable order \u2014 completed](evidence/09-completion.md): implementation `7f4eac0`; **469 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, wheel/install and installed CLI graph/status passed. [21 final-suite dependency scenarios and installed graph](evidence/09-fixture-observations.json) and [actual check output](evidence/09-checks.log) verify explicit selection, stable numeric ready order, one baseline, current verified integration bases, dependency unlocking only after Done, per-ticket repairs/evidence, and complete run/status states/revisions. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no blockers or optional suggestions; Spec independently passed three cases. All six criteria are verified; no unchecked criteria or required unresolved items remain. Continuing unrelated work after blocks remains ticket 20; live Codex/role guidance, OS enforcement, concurrency and recovery remain later work.\n\n- [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan \u2014 completed](evidence/10-completion.md): implementation `70a0122`; custom `grill-to-tickets` and one shared planning reference, upstream unchanged. [Actual checks and independent reviews](evidence/10-checks.log) and [raw isolated planning observations](evidence/10-planning-observations.json) verify joint spec/proposal feedback, targeted confirmation, declined-publication preservation, and an approved five-ticket 2/2/1 QA bundle with worker override. Official skill validation, 14 source links/anchors, 199 example links/anchors and whitespace passed; separate fresh High Spec/Standards reviews each found zero blockers or optional suggestions. Initial example execution and subsequent final-source numbering audits are distinguished in the evidence. All six criteria are verified; runtime/skill compatibility remains ticket 27. Next is ready M1 ticket 11; no milestone acceptance is implied.\n\n- [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints \u2014 completed](evidence/11-completion.md): implementation `552fcd6`; both development wrappers now enforce approved milestone/order/prerequisite eligibility and distinguish implementation, QA/waiting and final-acceptance handoffs. [Actual checks](evidence/11-checks.log), [static validation](evidence/11-static/) and [three isolated outputs](evidence/11-handoff-observations.json) passed; separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/11-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/11-review-standards.md) reviews found zero blockers or optional suggestions. All six criteria are verified. Upstream/shared planning guidance and unrelated tracker edits are preserved. Next eligible work is M1 ticket 12; M1 and final feature QA remain unaccepted. No runtime capability or acceptance is claimed.\n\n- [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone \u2014 completed](evidence/12-completion.md): implementation `14cafef`; optional versioned runtime plans validate/capture fixed membership, final coverage, QA and settings before execution. [499 passing tests and required checks](evidence/12-checks.log) and [78 retained final-run observations](evidence/12-fixture-observations.json), including 30 new milestone cases, verify first-group-only feature integration and durable preparation-pending with later tickets unstarted and dev unchanged. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/12-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/12-review-standards.md) reviews each found zero blockers or optional suggestions. All five criteria are verified. Ticket 13 is next in M1; candidate preparation, promotion, continuation, and M1/final acceptance remain pending. Captured role settings do not claim live enforcement.\n\n- [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate \u2014 completed](evidence/13-completion.md): implementation `19ea4f1`; current feature/dev candidates receive a separate exact regression gate and identity-bound QA request, preserving ticket gates, dev and later-group waiting. [509 passing tests and required checks](evidence/13-checks.log) and [88 final-run observations](evidence/13-fixture-observations.json) verify passing/failed/changed-base requests, source/ref invalidation and conflict-resolution renewal requirements. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/13-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/13-review-standards.md) reviews found zero blockers; Standards recorded one optional duplicate status assertion cleanup. All five criteria are verified. Ticket 14 is next in M1; approval consumption/promotion, continuation, and M1/final acceptance remain pending. Source-changing resolutions stop for renewed checks/reviews; no automatic conflict-repair orchestration is claimed.\n\n- [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue \u2014 completed](evidence/14-completion.md): implementation `29fb556`; exact separate decision matching, indefinite observable QA waits, atomic expected-old dev/feature promotion and ordered next-group execution are complete. [524 passing tests and required checks](evidence/14-checks.log) and [103 final observations](evidence/14-fixture-observations.json) verify stale/replayed rejection, preserved external changes, worker/repair authority protection, aligned later work and final-only completion. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/14-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/14-review-standards.md) reviews found zero blockers; Standards retained one optional polling-helper consolidation. All six criteria are verified. Ticket 15 is next in M1; planned stop/continuation and M1/final human acceptance remain pending. Scripted fixture decisions do not accept the development milestone.\n\n- [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop \u2014 completed](evidence/15-completion.md): implementation `36ed3e7`, final repair `d11f0bc`; durable QA stop/new-process continuation, exact checkpoint/input/source/evidence/ref validation and exclusive run ownership are complete. [544 passing tests and required checks](evidence/15-repair1-check-results.json), [123 renewed observations](evidence/15-repair1-fixture-observations.json) and installed CLI success/invalidation establish final proof. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/15-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/15-review-standards.md) whole-diff reviews each found zero blockers or optional suggestions after STD15-01 was repaired and all required gates renewed. All five criteria are verified. **M1 required work is complete; M1 QA preparation and human acceptance are pending.** No development request/run/candidate/decision exists, and ticket 16/M2 remains gated. Fixture decisions do not accept the development milestone.\n",
-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/archive/oop-numbering-history.md": "# OOP amendment numbering and publication map\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v1.\n\nThe human explicitly requested that new OOP work be inserted as 16\u201318 and existing published open tickets shift to keep execution order sequential. Completed 01\u201315 and historical evidence keep their IDs. Existing stable R01\u2013R19 slice identifiers stay unchanged; O01\u2013O03 identify only the added refactor slices.\n\n| Previous published ID | Proposed ID | Slice | Title |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| New | 16 | O01 | [16: Own implementation-attempt transitions](../issues/16-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md) |\n| New | 17 | O02 | [17: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](../issues/17-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md) |\n| New | 18 | O03 | [18: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](../issues/18-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md) |\n| 16 | 19 | R07 | [19: Guide a human through milestone QA](../issues/19-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md) |\n| 17 | 20 | R08 | [20: Propose a versioned correction plan](../issues/20-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md) |\n| 18 | 21 | R09 | [21: Execute approved QA corrections](../issues/21-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md) |\n| 19 | 22 | R10 | [22: Operate the orchestrator in the background](../issues/22-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md) |\n| 20 | 23 | R11 | [23: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](../issues/23-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md) |\n| 21 | 24 | R12 | [24: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](../issues/24-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md) |\n| 22 | 25 | R13 | [25: Capture and deliver selected local skills](../issues/25-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md) |\n| 23 | 26 | R14 | [26: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](../issues/26-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md) |\n| 24 | 27 | R15 | [27: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](../issues/27-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md) |\n| 25 | 28 | R16 | [28: Run the early context-budget comparison](../issues/28-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md) |\n| 26 | 29 | R17 | [29: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](../issues/29-verify-role-write-boundaries.md) |\n| 27 | 30 | R18 | [30: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](../issues/30-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md) |\n| 28 | 31 | R19 | [31: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](../issues/31-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) |\n\n## Publication scope\n\nAfter approval of the complete bundle, publish the revised spec, proposal, milestones and feature index, three new issues, renamed 13 open issues and their synchronized current references. Preserve the prior canonical documents and 13 open issue bodies under `archive/before-oop-v1/` with their original identities and a provenance note for source revision `152b0c4577269789a419079c6261c69f9a0695fd`. Add this numbering map without overwriting the previous numbering-history record. Update current owner pointers in historical navigation only; leave historical requirement text, completed-ticket bodies, evidence logs, captured run inputs and previous decisions unchanged.\n\nCurrent references outside the feature's live authoring files, including a current execution handoff, must be checked at publication. Replace stale scheduling guidance with the new M1 scope or an explicit historical pointer. Do not rewrite historical or runtime identity claims merely because their numbers collide with new tickets.\n\nThe prior development plan had no explicit version identifier. `oop-v1` names this proposed amendment; it is not a retrospective version for old run inputs. The publication approval record must identify this exact draft bundle. Scope confirmation in this conversation is not approval of unseen ticket criteria.\n"
