-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/milestones.md": "# Development milestones \u2014 ownership amendment\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v2.\n\n## Eligibility and decisions\n\nCompleted 01\u201315 retain their evidence. New 16\u201320 extend M1 before its pending QA. After publication select prerequisite-ready work in the preferred order; each later milestone waits for explicit human acceptance of the previous one. Ticket completion, test results and plan approval are separate from human candidate acceptance. E1 remains an independent experiment immediately after verified 29; it does not gate release.\n\nDevelopment milestones in this document remain distinct from runtime milestones in disposable target repositories. No development request, candidate, decision or acceptance is fabricated here. Preserve active-run inputs and historical fixture identities.\n\n## Required release membership\n\n| Milestone | Required tickets in preferred order | Gate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| M1: A complete QA-controlled Git cycle | [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md), [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md), [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md), [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md), [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md), [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md), [16: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues/16-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md), [17: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](issues/17-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md), [18: Return clearly prepared inputs](issues/18-return-clearly-prepared-inputs.md), [19: Own the complete run lifecycle](is