-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/milestones.md": "# Development milestones \u2014 ownership and review amendment\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v2. **Draft revision:** review-process-1.\n\n## Eligibility and decisions\n\nCompleted 01\u201315 retain their evidence. M1 gains nine required tickets 16\u201324 before its still-unrequested QA. Review workflow/evaluation precedes the five refactors; later milestones wait for explicit human acceptance of the previous one. Required architecture assessments and disposition rules precede QA readiness, while review completion and review decisions never equal candidate acceptance. E1 remains independent, immediately after verified 34.\n\n## Required release membership\n\n| Milestone | Required tickets in preferred order | Gate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| M1: A complete QA-controlled Git cycle | [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md), [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md), [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md), [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md), [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md), [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md), [16: Record review work, findings and decisions](issues/16-record-review-work-findings-and-decisions.md), [17: Review ownership across affected modules](issues/17-review-ownership-across-affected-modules.md), [18: Gate development on cumulative architecture review](issues/18-gate-development-on-cumulative-architecture-review.md), [19: Evaluate reviewers on known and acceptable designs](issues/19-evaluate-reviewers-on-known-and-acceptable-designs.md), [20: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues