monstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) | Explicit human acceptance of M3 |\n\nEvery required ticket 10\u201334 and 36\u201338 has exactly one required membership (28 tickets, including completed 10\u201315). Completed baseline 01\u201309 remains intact. Ticket 35 belongs only to E1. M4 supplies final cumulative feature acceptance. Development milestones remain distinct from runtime fixture milestones.\n\n## M1: A complete QA-controlled Git cycle\n\n**Required tickets:** [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md), [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md), [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md), [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md), [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md), [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md), [16: Record review work, findings and decisions](issues/16-record-review-work-findings-and-decisions.md), [17: Review ownership across affected modules](issues/17-review-ownership-across-affected-modules.md), [18: Gate development on cumulative architecture review](issues/18-gate-development-on-cumulative-architecture-review.md), [19: Evaluate reviewers on known and acceptable designs](issues/19-evaluate-reviewers-on-known-and-acceptable-designs.md), [20: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues/20-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md), [21: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](issues/21-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md), [22: Return clearly prepared inputs](issues/22-return-clearly-prepared-inputs.md), [23: Own the complete run lifecycle](issues/23-own-the-complete-run-lifecycle.md), [24: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](issues/24-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** Use an isolated miniature tracker and actual development reviewer evaluation artifacts, then a disposable foreground scripted two-milestone target repository with the refactored final source. Include the nine new ticket outcomes, genuine pre-refactor checkpoint evidence and a cumulative all-file architecture assessment.\n\n**Human actions:** Follow a review concern through its immutable report, human/agent disposition, repair ticket/commit and verification. Inspect all declared evaluation cases, misses/false positives and guidance versions. Confirm risk-triggered/milestone assessments expose unresolved work, clean reviews progress, and changed source invalidates stale assessments. Inspect ownership reports for refactors 20\u201324. Then demonstrate first-group feature integration, exact tested QA request, stale-approval rejection, deliberate stop/new-process continuation without replay, exact human approval/promotion and final-only completion. Inspect invalid-input/failed-baseline and canonical restored-evidence invalidation observations.\n\n**Pass conditions:** All M1 work is verified; review records explain why code changed, meaningful decisions remain human-owned, the declared reviewer corpus meets its criteria, and cumulative architecture assessment has no unresolved in-scope blocker. Existing CLI/record/checkpoint compatibility and exact QA behavior remain intact. Scripted approvals and review completion do not accept the development milestone.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed source/feature/development/candidate revisions, plan/run/request identities, actual gate results, cumulative review scope/baseline, immutable reports and finding/decision history, observed human checks and explicit request-specific QA decision. Changed source or accepted corrections require renewed applicable review/candidate checks and human acceptance. Historical fixture decisions are not development milestone acceptance.\n\n## M2: An unattended operator workflow\n\n**Required tickets:** [25: Guide a human through milestone QA](issues/25-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md), [26: Propose a versioned correction plan](issues/26-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md), [27: Execute approved QA corrections](issues/27-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md), [28: Operate the orchestrator in the background](issues/28-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md), [29: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](issues/29-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** After M1 acceptance, use QA-session/correction guidance and a disposable plan with independent and dependent work; include a review-originated correction and separate operator sessions.\n\n**Human actions:** Inspect review findings/reasons alongside the candidate, request a correction and approve its amendment without accepting the candidate. Observe renewed QA, terminal-independent background operation, accurate status/logs, blocked-root/unrelated-success behavior, and cumulative architecture assessment before M2 QA.\n\n**Pass conditions:** Review dispositions, correction approval and exact candidate acceptance remain distinct. Background status is observational, independent work respects prerequisite/milestone gates, and significant unresolved findings prevent readiness under the shared review contract.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed source/feature/development/candidate revisions, plan/run/request identities, actual gate results, cumulative review scope/baseline, immutable reports and finding/decision history, observed human checks and explicit request-specific QA decision. Changed source or accepted corrections require renewed applicable review/candidate checks and human acceptance. Historical fixture decisions are not development milestone acceptance.\n\n## M3: Real agents with explicit guidance\n\n**Required tickets:** [30: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](issues/30-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md), [31: Capture and deliver selected local skills](issues/31-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md), [32: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](issues/32-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md), [33: Enforce traceable runtime review checkpoints](issues/33-enforce-traceable-runtime-review-checkpoints.md), [34: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](issues/34-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** After M2 acceptance, prepare scripted runtime review/decision cases and a tiny real-Codex plan using captured role guidance, a worker override, a seeded concern and an acceptable control.\n\n**Human actions:** Inspect actual captured/delivered ownership/review instructions, inspected scope, immutable reports, finding/decision history and independent role profiles. Observe scripted runtime blocking/stale/authority/continuation cases and a real cumulative assessment plus independent ticket reviews. Verify no consumable QA request appears with unresolved required review work. Schedule E1 immediately after verified 34.\n\n**Pass conditions:** Runtime review enforcement and actual real-agent instruction delivery/judgment are evidenced separately from M1 development evaluation. Human risk decisions and QA acceptance stay separate. E1 never gates release or supplies assumed model/context defaults.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed source/feature/development/candidate revisions, plan/run/request identities, actual gate results, cumulative review scope/baseline, immutable reports and finding/decision history, observed human checks and explicit request-specific QA decision. Changed source or accepted corrections require renewed applicable review/candidate checks and human acceptance. Historical fixture decisions are not development milestone acceptance.\n\n## M4: First usable release and final acceptance\n\n**Required tickets:** [36: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](issues/36-verify-role-write-boundaries.md), [37: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](issues/37-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md), [38: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](issues/38-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** After M3 acceptance, start from a clean installed checkout and disposable target with generated-plan and role/access evidence, linked review history and all prior accepted milestone assessments.\n\n**Human actions:** Operate the full planning, execution, review/decision, correction, background/status, deliberate stop/continue and exact QA/promotion cycle. Follow a concern from report through human rationale, implementation revision and independent verification. Inspect review-authority probes, final cumulative architecture assessment, unresolved/deferred findings and documented limitations.\n\n**Pass conditions:** All required tickets 10\u201334 and 36\u201338 and prior milestone acceptances are accounted for cumulatively; the final source has the required architecture assessment, exact tested candidate and explicit final human acceptance. Review completion, all ticket Done states and automated gates alone are insufficient.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed source/feature/development/candidate revisions, plan/run/request identities, actual gate results, cumulative review scope/baseline, immutable reports and finding/decision history, observed human checks and explicit request-specific QA decision. Changed source or accepted corrections require renewed applicable review/candidate checks and human acceptance. Historical fixture decisions are not development milestone acceptance.\n\n## E1: Independent early context experiment\n\n**Required tickets:** [35: Run the early context-budget comparison](issues/35-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md)\n\n**QA status:** Not yet requested or accepted.\n\n**QA setup:** Immediately after verified 34 supplies the real backend and usage/settings evidence, select experiment 35 independently of release work.\n\n**Human actions:** Review the controlled 100K/150K/200K/250K comparison, pressure case, active versus cumulative/cached usage, compaction behavior and measured quality/limitations. Keep reviewer effectiveness evidence distinct from this context-budget experiment.\n\n**Pass conditions:** Document actual enforcement/compaction/advisory limits and independent experiment acceptance without making E1 a release prerequisite or silently changing role/context defaults.\n\n**Acceptance evidence:** Retain assessed source/feature/development/candidate revisions, plan/run/request identities, actual gate results, cumulative review scope/baseline, immutable reports and finding/decision history, observed human checks and explicit request-specific QA decision. Changed source or accepted corrections require renewed applicable review/candidate checks and human acceptance. Historical fixture decisions are not development milestone acceptance.\n",
-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/README.md": "# Ticket harness \u2014 proposed ownership and review amendment\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v2. **Draft revision:** review-process-1.\n\nReview the [spec](spec.md), [complete ticket bodies/dependencies](ticket-proposal.md), [milestones](milestones.md), [numbering map](archive/oop-numbering-history.md), domain additions and supporting updates together. The human requested this expansion; complete-bundle publication approval is pending.\n\n## Implementation status\n\nCompleted 01\u201315 retain their IDs and evidence. New development review work 16\u201319 precedes five refactors 20\u201324 in M1; new runtime review enforcement 33 precedes real-agent work 34 in M3. Thirteen inherited open tickets are renumbered coherently, yielding23 proposed open tickets 16\u201338. M1 contains six completed 10\u201315 and nine new 16\u201324. Human M1 QA is not requested/accepted, and later milestones remain gated.\n\nAfter publication the next proposed implementation is16, backed by completed 10/11. Prefer ascending prerequisite-ready work, respecting human milestone acceptance. This draft launches no review evaluation, implementation or harness run.\n\n## Complete ticket index\n\n| ID and title | Prerequisites | Readiness/completion | Milestone |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [01: Complete one scripted ticket through every gate](issues/01-complete-one-scripted-ticket-cycle.md) | None | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [02: Reject invalid requirements before starting work](issues/02-reject-invalid-inputs-before-execution.md) | 01 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [03: Reject invalid agent reports and review evidence](issues/03-validate-agent-reports-and-review-evidence.md) | 01 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [04: Promote only the exact verified candidate](issues/04-promote-only-the-verified-candidate.md) | 01 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [05: Repair rejected submissions within a bounded allowance](issues/05-repair-rejected-submissions-within-budget.md) | 03, 04 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [06: Stop for decisions outside approved contracts](issues/06-surface-human-decisions-without-retrying.md) | 05 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [07: Report optional review suggestions without rework](issues/07-report-optional-suggestions-without-repair.md) | 05 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [08: Stop stalled assignments and check processes](issues/08-stop-timed-out-process-trees.md) | 05 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [09: Execute verified dependencies in a stable order](issues/09-execute-dependencies-sequentially.md) | 02 | completed | Completed baseline |\n| [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan](issues/10-produce-approved-harness-inputs-with-planning-skill.md) | 09 | completed | M1 |\n| [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints](issues/11-stop-development-handoffs-at-qa-milestones.md) | 10 | completed | M1 |\n| [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone](issues/12-execute-only-the-current-qa-milestone.md) | 10 | completed | M1 |\n| [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate](issues/13-prepare-a-tested-feature-to-dev-candidate.md) | 12 | completed | M1 |\n| [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue](issues/14-promote-only-the-human-approved-milestone.md) | 13 | completed | M1 |\n| [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop](issues/15-continue-from-a-planned-qa-checkpoint.md) | 14 | completed | M1 |\n| [16: Record review work, findings and decisions](issues/16-record-review-work-findings-and-decisions.md) | 10, 11 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [17: Review ownership across affected modules](issues/17-review-ownership-across-affected-modules.md) | 16 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [18: Gate development on cumulative architecture review](issues/18-gate-development-on-cumulative-architecture-review.md) | 16, 17 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [19: Evaluate reviewers on known and acceptable designs](issues/19-evaluate-reviewers-on-known-and-acceptable-designs.md) | 17, 18 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [20: Own implementation-attempt transitions](issues/20-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md) | 05, 06, 19 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [21: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](issues/21-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md) | 20 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [22: Return clearly prepared inputs](issues/22-return-clearly-prepared-inputs.md) | 02, 12, 19 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [23: Own the complete run lifecycle](issues/23-own-the-complete-run-lifecycle.md) | 15, 21, 22 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [24: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](issues/24-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md) | 15, 23 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M1 |\n| [25: Guide a human through milestone QA](issues/25-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md) | 10, 14 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [26: Propose a versioned correction plan](issues/26-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md) | 10, 25 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [27: Execute approved QA corrections](issues/27-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md) | 15, 26 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [28: Operate the orchestrator in the background](issues/28-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md) | 15 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [29: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](issues/29-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md) | 12, 06 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M2 |\n| [30: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](issues/30-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md) | 03, 19 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [31: Capture and deliver selected local skills](issues/31-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md) | 10, 30 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [32: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](issues/32-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md) | 31, 19 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [33: Enforce traceable runtime review checkpoints](issues/33-enforce-traceable-runtime-review-checkpoints.md) | 19, 24, 30, 31, 32 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [34: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](issues/34-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md) | 15, 32, 08, 33 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M3 |\n| [35: Run the early context-budget comparison](issues/35-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md) | 34 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | E1 |\n| [36: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](issues/36-verify-role-write-boundaries.md) | 25, 34 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M4 |\n| [37: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](issues/37-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md) | 10, 27, 31 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M4 |\n| [38: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](issues/38-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) | 11, 28, 29, 36, 37, 07 | ready-for-agent (proposed) | M4 |\n\nPreferred groups: M1 10\u201324, M2 25\u201329, M3 30\u201334, independent E1 35 immediately after verified 34, final M4 36\u201338 after M3 acceptance. Review work completion, findings dispositioned, implementation Done and human QA acceptance remain distinct. Review work-item IDs are separate from this implementation-ticket sequence. E1 never gates release.\n\n## History\n\nPreserve the [prior approved authoring bundle](archive/before-oop-v2/README.md), original open issues and old root handoff before replacing live authoring files. The [mapping](archive/oop-numbering-history.md) records published and previous-draft identities. The earlier unapproved oop-v2 snapshot is retained under `drafts/oop-v2-before-review-process/`; oop-v1 remains prior planning history. Historical completion evidence below remains verbatim, with its original next-ticket/milestone statements scoped to that time.\n\n## Agent context policy\n\n- Use GPT-6.1 Sol as requested, with one fresh context for each implementation, review, or repair assignment.\n- Target at most **250,000 tokens of active context per agent**, including instructions, relevant source, tool results, reasoning/output retained in context, and room to finish verification and the handoff.\n- This is a per-agent context constraint, not a cumulative per-ticket usage budget. Reprocessing cached input across requests can make cumulative usage much larger than the currently occupied context.\n- Read the assigned issue and its scoped spec references first. Follow the repository's glossary/ADR instructions, discover the affected source, and pull extra references when necessary. Sibling transcripts and entire upstream skill libraries are not default inputs.\n- Keep headroom for debugging and final checks. If the bounded outcome will not fit, preserve useful work and report the evidence and proposed split before expanding the assignment.\n- No numerical implementation-usage estimate is claimed before measurements exist. These slices are scoped by observable outcomes and the context required to understand them.\n- The current local Codex catalog reports 500,000 nominal tokens and a 95% effective-window setting for gpt-6.1-sol; the inspected session reports a 475,000 effective window. The requested 8M figure was clarified to a 250K agent target after distinguishing cumulative usage from active context.\n- The 250K target guides the agents implementing these issues. Configurable runtime context controls and empirical comparison belong to the early live-backend experiment below; this document does not claim that a new hard runtime cap has already been implemented.\n\n## Worker handoff\n\nStart from the latest integrated prerequisite work. Read the current interface and evidence needed for this issue rather than replaying prior development conversations. Work on this issue's acceptance behavior and test at the public CLI/Git/report seam described by the spec.\n\nReturn a compact report with the outcome, commit references/changed files, actual check commands and exit results, and remaining decisions or risks. Preserve verbose logs as artifacts and link to them when needed.\n\nDuring approved harness execution, source specs and tickets remain unchanged and the harness owns execution records. A ready-for-agent label or published ticket alone does not start a run. Concurrency, arbitrary interruption/crash recovery, hosted PRs, and email remain deferred. Planned-QA checkpoint stop/continuation is implemented by ticket 15; development M1 and final feature human acceptance remain pending.\n\n## Early context-budget experiment\n\n[35: Compare configurable 100K\u2013250K agent context limits](issues/35-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md) is ready for execution immediately after issue 34 supplies the verified real Codex cycle, configured roles, and usage artifacts. Prioritize it then; it does not require the final release demonstration, multi-ticket scheduling, the planning skill, or the later access-boundary probes. It is a separate early experiment, not an additional first-release completion gate.\n\nThe user requested configurable per-agent limits of **100K, 150K, 200K, and 250K**. Compare the same workload, model, role reasoning settings, and acceptance checks at each setting. Record verified results, repair behavior, observed active context, compaction/handoff behavior, elapsed time, and cumulative/cached usage separately.\n\nUse a short control to verify configuration and reporting, plus a task-relevant case that can approach the configured context thresholds. If all runs remain below 100K, they cannot establish the comparative effects of the larger budgets.\n\nVerify whether the installed backend enforces a hard limit, applies a compaction threshold, or only supports advisory guidance. Report that distinction explicitly rather than interpreting cumulative input totals as window occupancy or claiming unsupported enforcement.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\n- [01: Complete one scripted ticket through every gate \u2014 completed](evidence/01-completion.md): implementation `b09e324`, final implementation `1666920`; 8 passing tests and passing checks; separate independent Spec and Standards reviews completed. [Actual fixture observations](evidence/01-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/01-complete-one-scripted-ticket-cycle.md#comments) record the passing and rejected runs. Later tickets and first-release completion remain outstanding.\n\n- [02: Reject invalid requirements before starting work \u2014 completed](evidence/02-completion.md): checkpoint `855a4c8`, review fixes `dfdb1a6` and final implementation `b11fd20`; 73 passing tests and passing checks; separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews passed. [Actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/02-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/02-reject-invalid-inputs-before-execution.md#comments) provide criterion-specific evidence. Eligibility validation is complete; dependency scheduling and later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [03: Reject invalid agent reports and review evidence \u2014 completed](evidence/03-completion.md): checkpoint `5b04187`, review fixes `2a27565` and final implementation `07094fa`; 256 passing tests and passing documented checks; independent Spec and Standards reviews passed with no remaining findings. [Actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/03-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/03-validate-agent-reports-and-review-evidence.md#comments) verify all six criteria. Report validation is complete; the subsequent transaction slice is recorded below. Repairs, broader human-decision handling, and later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [04: Promote only the exact verified candidate \u2014 completed](evidence/04-completion.md): checkpoint `dc27eb2`, final implementation/review fixes `8d345bd`; **304 passing tests** and passing documented checks; separate independent Spec and Standards re-reviews passed with no outstanding findings. [16 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/04-fixture-observations.json) and the [ticket completion comment](issues/04-promote-only-the-verified-candidate.md#comments) verify all six criteria. Approved-input/state integrity, source approval invalidation, and exact candidate promotion are complete within the documented process-boundary limits. Automatic repairs and later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [05: Repair rejected submissions within a bounded allowance \u2014 completed](evidence/05-completion.md): implementation `34a49b7`; **362 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, packaging/installed CLI, and [20 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/05-fixture-observations.json) passed. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no issues. All six criteria verify configurable bounded repairs, fresh assignments with preserved rejection evidence, renewed exact-revision gates, and preserved Blocked/incomplete exhaustion. No unchecked criteria or unresolved ticket-05 items remain. Human-decision handling and neighboring later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [06: Stop for decisions outside approved contracts \u2014 completed](evidence/06-completion.md): implementation `dc1018e`; **399 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, packaging/installed CLI run/status, and [19 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/06-fixture-observations.json) passed. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no issues; Spec independently passed all 37 decision tests. All five criteria verify validated implementation/either-axis decisions, precise preserved contract/evidence/work handoffs, immediate stopping with repair allowance available, unchanged approved inputs/integration, and matching status/final output with accurate initial/later-repair history. No unchecked criteria or unresolved ticket-06 items remain. Optional-suggestion reporting and other later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [07: Report optional review suggestions without rework \u2014 completed](evidence/07-completion.md): checkpoint `83d361d`; **421 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, packaging/installed CLI and [23 actual CLI/Git observations](evidence/07-fixture-observations.json) passed. Existing runtime behavior satisfied the ticket; 22 new cases and public contracts verify optional-only integration without consuming available repairs, full evidence/revision retention, mixed-finding repairs/exhaustion, changing suggestions across revisions, validation and human-decision compatibility. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no blockers; Spec independently passed 12 cases. Standards recorded one optional test-fixture consolidation suggestion. All five criteria are verified; no unchecked criteria or required unresolved items remain. Timeouts and neighboring later-ticket features remain outstanding.\n\n- [08: Stop stalled assignments and check processes \u2014 completed](evidence/08-completion.md): implementation `fbfc088`; **448 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, wheel/install and installed CLI passed. [27 actual timeout-test observations plus installed CLI smoke](evidence/08-fixture-observations.json) verify positive stage allowances, inherited process-group/child cleanup, partial output, timeout precedence over report claims/zero leader exits, fresh bounded repairs and exact integration, exhaustion, baseline/environment stopping and durable status evidence. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no blockers; Spec independently verified background-child cleanup after normal completion. Standards recorded optional S1 about streaming output to reduce memory use. All six criteria are verified; no unchecked criteria or required unresolved items remain. Scheduling/continuation, live Codex/role guidance, OS role enforcement and recovery remain later tickets.\n\n- [09: Execute verified dependencies in a stable order \u2014 completed](evidence/09-completion.md): implementation `7f4eac0`; **469 passing tests**, strict mypy, Ruff lint/format, whitespace, wheel/install and installed CLI graph/status passed. [21 final-suite dependency scenarios and installed graph](evidence/09-fixture-observations.json) and [actual check output](evidence/09-checks.log) verify explicit selection, stable numeric ready order, one baseline, current verified integration bases, dependency unlocking only after Done, per-ticket repairs/evidence, and complete run/status states/revisions. Separate fresh Spec and Standards reviews found no blockers or optional suggestions; Spec independently passed three cases. All six criteria are verified; no unchecked criteria or required unresolved items remain. Continuing unrelated work after blocks remains ticket 20; live Codex/role guidance, OS enforcement, concurrency and recovery remain later work.\n\n- [10: Turn one grilling session into an approved plan \u2014 completed](evidence/10-completion.md): implementation `70a0122`; custom `grill-to-tickets` and one shared planning reference, upstream unchanged. [Actual checks and independent reviews](evidence/10-checks.log) and [raw isolated planning observations](evidence/10-planning-observations.json) verify joint spec/proposal feedback, targeted confirmation, declined-publication preservation, and an approved five-ticket 2/2/1 QA bundle with worker override. Official skill validation, 14 source links/anchors, 199 example links/anchors and whitespace passed; separate fresh High Spec/Standards reviews each found zero blockers or optional suggestions. Initial example execution and subsequent final-source numbering audits are distinguished in the evidence. All six criteria are verified; runtime/skill compatibility remains ticket 27. Next is ready M1 ticket 11; no milestone acceptance is implied.\n\n- [11: Stop development handoffs at human checkpoints \u2014 completed](evidence/11-completion.md): implementation `552fcd6`; both development wrappers now enforce approved milestone/order/prerequisite eligibility and distinguish implementation, QA/waiting and final-acceptance handoffs. [Actual checks](evidence/11-checks.log), [static validation](evidence/11-static/) and [three isolated outputs](evidence/11-handoff-observations.json) passed; separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/11-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/11-review-standards.md) reviews found zero blockers or optional suggestions. All six criteria are verified. Upstream/shared planning guidance and unrelated tracker edits are preserved. Next eligible work is M1 ticket 12; M1 and final feature QA remain unaccepted. No runtime capability or acceptance is claimed.\n\n- [12: Execute only the first eligible milestone \u2014 completed](evidence/12-completion.md): implementation `14cafef`; optional versioned runtime plans validate/capture fixed membership, final coverage, QA and settings before execution. [499 passing tests and required checks](evidence/12-checks.log) and [78 retained final-run observations](evidence/12-fixture-observations.json), including 30 new milestone cases, verify first-group-only feature integration and durable preparation-pending with later tickets unstarted and dev unchanged. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/12-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/12-review-standards.md) reviews each found zero blockers or optional suggestions. All five criteria are verified. Ticket 13 is next in M1; candidate preparation, promotion, continuation, and M1/final acceptance remain pending. Captured role settings do not claim live enforcement.\n\n- [13: Present a tested feature-to-dev candidate \u2014 completed](evidence/13-completion.md): implementation `19ea4f1`; current feature/dev candidates receive a separate exact regression gate and identity-bound QA request, preserving ticket gates, dev and later-group waiting. [509 passing tests and required checks](evidence/13-checks.log) and [88 final-run observations](evidence/13-fixture-observations.json) verify passing/failed/changed-base requests, source/ref invalidation and conflict-resolution renewal requirements. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/13-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/13-review-standards.md) reviews found zero blockers; Standards recorded one optional duplicate status assertion cleanup. All five criteria are verified. Ticket 14 is next in M1; approval consumption/promotion, continuation, and M1/final acceptance remain pending. Source-changing resolutions stop for renewed checks/reviews; no automatic conflict-repair orchestration is claimed.\n\n- [14: Consume approval, promote, and continue \u2014 completed](evidence/14-completion.md): implementation `29fb556`; exact separate decision matching, indefinite observable QA waits, atomic expected-old dev/feature promotion and ordered next-group execution are complete. [524 passing tests and required checks](evidence/14-checks.log) and [103 final observations](evidence/14-fixture-observations.json) verify stale/replayed rejection, preserved external changes, worker/repair authority protection, aligned later work and final-only completion. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/14-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/14-review-standards.md) reviews found zero blockers; Standards retained one optional polling-helper consolidation. All six criteria are verified. Ticket 15 is next in M1; planned stop/continuation and M1/final human acceptance remain pending. Scripted fixture decisions do not accept the development milestone.\n\n- [15: Continue after a deliberate QA stop \u2014 completed](evidence/15-completion.md): implementation `36ed3e7`, final repair `d11f0bc`; durable QA stop/new-process continuation, exact checkpoint/input/source/evidence/ref validation and exclusive run ownership are complete. [544 passing tests and required checks](evidence/15-repair1-check-results.json), [123 renewed observations](evidence/15-repair1-fixture-observations.json) and installed CLI success/invalidation establish final proof. Separate fresh High [Spec](evidence/15-review-spec.md) and [Standards](evidence/15-review-standards.md) whole-diff reviews each found zero blockers or optional suggestions after STD15-01 was repaired and all required gates renewed. All five criteria are verified. **M1 required work is complete; M1 QA preparation and human acceptance are pending.** No development request/run/candidate/decision exists, and ticket 16/M2 remains gated. Fixture decisions do not accept the development milestone.\n",
-    ".scratch/ticket-harness/archive/oop-numbering-history.md": "# Ownership and review amendment numbering map\n\n**Draft \u2014 unapproved. Plan version:** oop-v2. **Draft revision:** review-process-1.\n\nCompleted 01\u201315 keep their IDs and evidence. Four development review tickets now precede the five refactors in M1; one runtime review-enforcement ticket precedes real agents in M3. Published old 16\u201323 become25\u201332; old 24\u201328 become34\u201338. The immediately previous unapproved oop-v2 draft is preserved under `drafts/oop-v2-before-review-process/`; its draft 16\u201328 shift by4 and draft 29\u201333 by5. No draft ID is an approved historical implementation identity.\n\n| Previous published ID | Previous oop-v2 draft ID | Current proposed ID | Stable slice | Title |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| New | New | 16 | RV01 | [16: Record review work, findings and decisions](../issues/16-record-review-work-findings-and-decisions.md) |\n| New | New | 17 | RV02 | [17: Review ownership across affected modules](../issues/17-review-ownership-across-affected-modules.md) |\n| New | New | 18 | RV03 | [18: Gate development on cumulative architecture review](../issues/18-gate-development-on-cumulative-architecture-review.md) |\n| New | New | 19 | RV04 | [19: Evaluate reviewers on known and acceptable designs](../issues/19-evaluate-reviewers-on-known-and-acceptable-designs.md) |\n| New | 16 | 20 | O01 | [20: Own implementation-attempt transitions](../issues/20-own-implementation-attempt-transitions.md) |\n| New | 17 | 21 | O02 | [21: Own ticket execution and bounded repairs](../issues/21-own-ticket-execution-and-bounded-repairs.md) |\n| New | 18 | 22 | O04 | [22: Return clearly prepared inputs](../issues/22-return-clearly-prepared-inputs.md) |\n| New | 19 | 23 | O05 | [23: Own the complete run lifecycle](../issues/23-own-the-complete-run-lifecycle.md) |\n| New | 20 | 24 | O03 | [24: Own milestone review and checkpoint continuation](../issues/24-own-milestone-review-and-checkpoint-continuation.md) |\n| 16 | 21 | 25 | R07 | [25: Guide a human through milestone QA](../issues/25-guide-and-record-human-milestone-qa.md) |\n| 17 | 22 | 26 | R08 | [26: Propose a versioned correction plan](../issues/26-propose-versioned-qa-corrections.md) |\n| 18 | 23 | 27 | R09 | [27: Execute approved QA corrections](../issues/27-execute-approved-qa-corrections.md) |\n| 19 | 24 | 28 | R10 | [28: Operate the orchestrator in the background](../issues/28-operate-the-harness-in-the-background.md) |\n| 20 | 25 | 29 | R11 | [29: Continue independent work inside the current milestone](../issues/29-continue-independent-work-after-blocks.md) |\n| 21 | 26 | 30 | R12 | [30: Supply coherent design guidance to Standards review](../issues/30-supply-combined-design-guidance-to-standards-review.md) |\n| 22 | 27 | 31 | R13 | [31: Capture and deliver selected local skills](../issues/31-capture-and-deliver-selected-local-skills.md) |\n| 23 | 28 | 32 | R14 | [32: Deliver focused implementation and Spec contexts](../issues/32-deliver-focused-implementation-and-spec-review-contexts.md) |\n| New | New | 33 | RV05 | [33: Enforce traceable runtime review checkpoints](../issues/33-enforce-traceable-runtime-review-checkpoints.md) |\n| 24 | 29 | 34 | R15 | [34: Complete the workflow with real Codex roles](../issues/34-run-a-real-codex-ticket-cycle.md) |\n| 25 | 30 | 35 | R16 | [35: Run the early context-budget comparison](../issues/35-compare-configurable-agent-context-limits.md) |\n| 26 | 31 | 36 | R17 | [36: Verify runtime write and approval boundaries](../issues/36-verify-role-write-boundaries.md) |\n| 27 | 32 | 37 | R18 | [37: Run a generated approved plan through the runtime](../issues/37-run-a-generated-plan-through-the-runtime.md) |\n| 28 | 33 | 38 | R19 | [38: Demonstrate the revised first usable release](../issues/38-demonstrate-the-first-usable-release.md) |\n\n## Publication scope\n\nPublish only after approval of this complete review-process-1 bundle: revised spec/proposal/milestones/index, nine new M1 issues and one new M3 issue, thirteen renumbered inherited issues with explicit review additions, numbering history and exact supporting reference/handoff/glossary updates. Before replacement, archive prior canonical documents, original thirteen open issue bodies and root handoff under `archive/before-oop-v2/`, retaining their original source `152b0c4577269789a419079c6261c69f9a0695fd` and identities. Existing unchanged criteria remain intact except reference renumbering; added review criteria are disclosed in the proposal and manifest.\n\nRecheck source hashes, worktree and active-run immutability before publication. Keep original reports, completed tickets, evidence, historical decisions and captured inputs unchanged. Update only current-owner navigation in existing historical indexes. This local authoring amendment launches no implementation, review evaluation, run or QA acceptance and authorizes no push or external publication.\n"
